  "step_3": "The decision reason is based on variance, which is not mentioned or considered in the verbal report. The individual instead focuses on the probability of receiving money, noting that 0.2% is better than 0.1%. This is a different reasoning process (probability-based preference) than the variance-based one. Even though the individual ends up choosing Lottery A (which has lower variance), the justification provided does not reference variance or any calculation or comparison of variance. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process. The individual did not apply the rule of preferring the lottery with smaller variance. The reasoning is clearly distinct from the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

